    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2LsmML8L7aw9coNUrrWP8iz)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #508; #496 and #498 are already merged. No other open PR is needed first.\n- Touches `sp-batch-report` and `sp-bibprocess` (docs in `sp-batch-report.org` and `sp-academic.org`, tests of the lint, long keys and litnote meta).\n- One PR for the three points: they share the new question helper, so splitting would conflict.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-vp77bk`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Cause of the lost help line: the batch questions (`a/g/s/q`, `d`, `u`) were `read-char-choice` prompts, so a long prompt replaced the echo-area hints of the report.\n  - New `sp-batch-report-ask` shows the question as the same two-row help line (keys with their descriptions, plus a note line such as \"Batch 1 of 3\").\n  - `n`, `p`, `TAB`, `S-TAB` and scrolling still work while it waits, so you can look through the batch before you answer (`sp-batch-report-ask-moves`).\n  - Used by `sp-batch-report--ask-batch` (all `sp-batch-process`-style commands) and by every BibTeX lint batch question: author names, notes and surnames, duplicates, long keys.\n  - `n` is no longer an answer: in steps 2 and 3 \"normalise in the field\" is `f`.\n- Merging variants of one author (`sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge`, step 4):\n  - one group at a time, the report scrolls to it; `RET` takes the proposed name, `1`-`9` take that variant, `e` types a name.\n  - `n` and `p` step to the next or previous group (as in the report), `c` clears a choice, `f` finishes, `q` or `C-g` stops.\n- Step 1 of the author names (`Last, First`):\n  - new `o` in the batch question: pick the entries to fix (comma separated, with completion); the others are not dropped, they come again in the next run.\n  - new option `sp-bibtex-lint-pick-first` (default nil): ask which names to fix before every batch of that step.\n\n## Tests (batch Emacs 29.3, container)\n\n- `sp-bibprocess-lint`: 111 of 111 pass (new: merge ask with digits, `n`/`p`, clear/finish; `o` and the option; the ask helper runs moves while waiting).\n- `sp-bibtex-long-keys`, `sp-batch-report-view`: all pass.\n- `sp-litnotes-meta` and `sp-batch-report`: the same 3 and 4 failures as on `main` (Org/packages missing in the container), no new ones.\n- Not run: the GUI, the real vault.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors`, press `A`: the batch question is the two-row help line at the bottom, not a one-line prompt\n- [ ] While it waits, `n`/`p` move in the report, `TAB` folds, `C-v`/`M-v` scroll; an unknown key only beeps\n- [ ] Step 1: `o`, pick two names with completion, `a`... only those change; the others show up in the next run and are not in \"dropped\"\n- [ ] `(setq sp-bibtex-lint-pick-first t)`: step 1 asks which names to fix first; empty answer fixes all\n- [ ] Steps 2 and 3: `f` normalises in the field, `l` adds an alias, `e` asks per name, `n` does not answer\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` on a file with variants: the report scrolls to each group; `2` takes the second variant, `p` goes back, `n` skips a group, `f` finishes, then the yes-or-no and the write\n- [ ] `C-g` or `q` in the merge stops with nothing written\n- [ ] Another `sp-batch-report-run-batches` command (litnote meta fill-all, convert): batch question is the help line, `a/c/s/g/q` still work\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-keys` and the duplicates fix: questions use the help line\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA9pvREDF2uyWN7wMC)_",
